  abstract = {The concept of a chain of ROVs has been introduced as a potential solution for operations in shallow waters or restricted areas. Previous research has focused on controlling pairs of ROVs, with control signals propagated between pairs to regulate the entire chain. In this paper, we propose a novel approach using a Model Predictive Control (MPC) strategy to manage a chain of n tethered ROVs as a single cohesive system, considering all operational constraints. The tether is modeled as a catenary curve while the ROVs are governed by dynamic equations based on Fossen's model. This approach enables the development of a reactive planning system to handle obstacles in the vicinity of the tether, ensuring robust and efficient navigation.},
